-- test: ADR 0067 amendment (2026-10-06), B08_fold_with_k: a T value decided by comparing T values goes where a value of T is expected (a lambda, a higher-order function, a function result, an `edit` binding or a field of the body), which edition 0.2 rejects in the generic body; the leak is rejected there, an accepted cost, since accepting it soundly would need re-checking lambdas (spec/07 §7 rule 8, #92)
-- spec: spec/07 §7
-- expect: error U4001 at src/b08_fold_with_k.una:7:109
-- expect: error U4001 at src/b08_fold_with_k.una:9:34
module b08_fold_with_k

apply[T](a: T, b: T, p: T, q: T, k: fn(T) -> Int) -> Int = [if a == b then p else q].fold(initial: 0, step: fn(acc, x) -> acc + k(x))

pub leak(s: secret Int) -> Int = apply([s], b: [0], p: [], q: [1, 2], k: fn(xs) -> xs.len)
